Subject: [PATCH] tls: ask for server handshake padding as Chrome does

Google Chrome turns on AddTLSServerHandshakePadding through a field trial,
and its ClientHello asks for 4000 bytes. This build runs no field trials, so its
ClientHello lacked the server_padding extension (0x12e0) and the JA4
fingerprint read t13d1517h2_8daaf6152771_cb7bf5808d99, which is Chrome 150's,
where Chrome 155 reads t13d1518h2_8daaf6152771_4980c97edce0. The feature
is now on by default with the 4000-byte request, in persona and host mode
alike, because the TLS stack is the same in both.

diff --git a/net/base/features.cc b/net/base/features.cc
index 91baaef..a2c4e25 100644
--- a/net/base/features.cc
+++ b/net/base/features.cc
@@ -992,13 +992,18 @@ BASE_FEATURE_PARAM(std::string,
                    &kEnablePrivateVerificationTokens,
                    "");
 
-BASE_FEATURE(kAddTLSServerHandshakePadding, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+// Apostate: on, asking for 4000 bytes, as Google Chrome turns it on through a
+// field trial. This build runs no field trials, so with Chromium's default the
+// ClientHello lacked the server_padding extension (0x12e0) that stable Chrome
+// sends since 152, and its JA4 read t13d1517h2 where Chrome's reads t13d1518h2.
+// 4000 is the length Chrome's own ClientHello asks for.
+BASE_FEATURE(kAddTLSServerHandshakePadding, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 BASE_FEATURE_PARAM(int,
                    kAddTLSServerHandshakePaddingBytes,
                    &kAddTLSServerHandshakePadding,
                    "AddTLSServerHandshakePaddingBytes",
-                   0);
+                   4000);
 
 bool IsDnsPlatformSupported() {
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
